{
  "id": "a1-tener",
  "slug": "tener-have-age-needs",
  "title": "Tener: to have, age, feelings and obligation",
  "unit": "A1",
  "group": "Grammar",
  "order": 22,
  "summary": "Tengo, tienes, tiene… and the many things Spanish 'has' instead of 'is'.",
  "focus": "Conjugation of tener; tener + años / hambre / que + infinitive; necesitar",
  "prerequisites": [
    "a1-regular-er-ir-present"
  ],
  "content": "## Tener is irregular\n\n| | tener (to have) |\n|---|---|\n| yo | **tengo** |\n| tú | tienes |\n| él / ella / usted | tiene |\n| nosotros/as | tenemos |\n| vosotros/as | tenéis |\n| ellos / ellas / ustedes | tienen |\n\nThe **yo** form has a **g** (*tengo*), and *e* becomes *ie* in three forms (tú, él/ella/usted, ellos/ellas/ustedes). *Nosotros* and *vosotros* are regular.\n\n## Possession\n\n- *Tengo dos hermanos.* (I have two brothers.)\n- *¿Tienes coche?* (Do you have a car? There is no article for the general idea.)\n\n## Age, hunger, cold: things you 'have'\n\nSpanish uses **tener + noun** where English uses *to be*:\n\n| Spanish | English |\n|---|---|\n| tener … años | to be … years old |\n| tener hambre / sed | to be hungry / thirsty |\n| tener frío / calor | to be cold / hot |\n| tener sueño | to be sleepy |\n| tener miedo | to be afraid |\n| tener prisa | to be in a hurry |\n| tener razón | to be right |\n\n- *Tengo veinte años.* (I'm twenty.)\n- *¿Tienes hambre?* (Are you hungry?)\n- *Tenemos mucho frío.* (We're very cold. Use *mucho*, not *muy*, because *frío* is a noun here.)\n\n## Tener que: obligation\n\n**tener que + infinitive** means to have to: *Tengo que trabajar.* (I have to work.) *Tienes que estudiar más.* (You have to study more.)\n\n**Necesitar** (to need) is a regular -ar verb: *Necesito un café. Necesitamos tiempo.*",
